{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "expand-multiyear-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.44: the `expand-multiyear` run computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE through `moves-onroad.esm`. It is `expand-day`'s weekday run at TWO calendar years, 2015 and 2020, and it is the first RunSpec in this tree whose `runspecyear` has more than one row.\n\nWHAT IT WAITS ON: the calendar year is the run's last scalar. `run_yearID` is a `run_rows` faq that sums `rsy_yearID` over `runspecyear_rows`, so at two years it is 4035 and every quantity keyed by it finds nothing. The forward closure from it reaches 395 of `onroad/model.esm`'s 1,036 equations, against the month's 32 and the source type's 125 when those were priced (PLAN.md §7.3.44).\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES, which §23 asks for before a dimension is called covered.\n\n* THE YEAR AXIS AT TWO VALUES. `MOVESOutput` is 241 rows: 125 cohorts at 2020, equal cell for cell to `expand-day`'s weekday block, and 116 at 2015, whose model years run 1975 to 2015. Nothing at 2015 is shared with 2020 but the age: the cohort's model year is the calendar year less its age, so every rate keyed by model year, the age distribution, the population, the VMT and the fuel year all move with it.\n\nTHE THIRTEEN SELECTIONS, ONE BINDING AND THE ORACLE are everything this document carries. `n_outputRate` is 241, one emitted block over both years' cohorts.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "expand-multiyear"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-multiyear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecyear.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "2 ROWS, yearID 2015 and 2020, AND THAT IS WHY THIS RUN IS HERE. Every other RunSpec in this tree selects one calendar year, 2020, so a model that read the year as a run-level scalar passed the whole suite. Both are base years (`year.isBaseYear` 'Y'), so neither needs the population or VMT growth fold (docs/esm-conventions.md §15).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecmonth": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-multiyear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecmonth.parquet"
      },
